{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121081","id":4012025261,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7vIqWt","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121081","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121081.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121081.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121081","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121081/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121081/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121081/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/a66ae53ddeb03693d789dd8c0ad2435ab09f03d5","number":121081,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Skip key copy in untyped Dictionary accessors","user":{"login":"xczcxczxzcz","id":283870210,"node_id":"U_kgDOEOuEAg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/283870210?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xczcxczxzcz","html_url":"https://github.com/xczcxczxzcz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xczcxczxzcz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xczcxczxzcz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xczcxczxzcz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xczcxczxzcz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xczcxczxzcz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xczcxczxzcz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xczcxczxzcz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xczcxczxzcz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xczcxczxzcz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Every `Dictionary` accessor (`operator[]`, `getptr`, `get`, `get_valid`, `get_or_add`, `set`, `has`, `has_all`, `erase`) starts with `Variant key = p_key;`, copying the key so it can be passed to `typed_key.validate()`, which takes a non-const reference and may coerce the key for typed dictionaries.\n\nFor an untyped dictionary (`typed_key.type == Variant::NIL`, the common case) `validate()` returns immediately without touching the key, so that copy is pure overhead. When the key is a `String`, `StringName`, `Array` or any `RefCounted`, the copy is an atomic refcount round-trip on every access.\n\nThis adds an untyped fast path to each accessor that uses `p_key` directly and skips the copy and the no-op validation. Typed dictionaries are unchanged: they still take the existing path and coerce keys exactly as before. Value handling is untouched.\n\n### Benchmark\n\nFixed-key tight loop from a `SceneTree` script, 8M iterations, best-of-5, release editor build, same machine (Windows, x86_64). Numbers include GDScript VM overhead, so the accessor-level improvement is a larger share than the wall-clock delta below.\n\n| operation | before | after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| string-key read (`dict[k]`) | 202 ns/op | 188 ns/op |\n| string-key write (`dict[k] = v`) | 181 ns/op | 164 ns/op |\n| string-key `k in dict` | 299 ns/op | 279 ns/op |\n| int-key read | 251 ns/op | 247 ns/op |\n| int-key `k in dict` | 246 ns/op | 237 ns/op |\n\nString keys benefit most (the removed atomic refcount traffic); integer keys still save the `Variant` construct/destruct.\n\n### Correctness\n\nA GDScript check script exercises String/StringName key equivalence, `get`/`get_valid`/`get_or_add`/`erase`/`has_all`, read-only rejection, and typed-dictionary key coercion (float coerced to int) and value handling. All assertions pass on the patched build.\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":tr